{"abstract":[{"text":"Snowplow’s trackers’ limits on one request, 25 events and 40,000 bytes of body, and an event","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of up to 150,000 bytes in a request of its own.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowBatchEncoder\/batchLimit","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"batchLimit"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/PropertyJSON\/documentation\/PropertyJSON\/BatchLimit","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"BatchLimit","preciseIdentifier":"s:12PropertyJSON10BatchLimitV"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Snowplow’s mobile trackers send at most 25 events and 40,000 bytes in a request by default,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and an event larger than that in a request of its own. A collector refuses a body over 2 MB","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with 413, and a request larger than its stream takes (192,000 bytes on SQS, 1 MB on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Kinesis, by default) becomes a failed event though the collector answers 200. So an event","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of up to 150,000 bytes of JSON is sent alone, within the smallest of those, and a larger one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is left out as ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/documentation\/SnowplowEncoding\/SnowplowEncodingError\/oversized(byteCount:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SnowplowEncoding\/document